#: ../../source/installation.rst:2
msgid "Installation"
msgstr "安装"

#: ../../source/installation.rst:9
msgid "Plugin for Claude Code"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/installation.rst:11
msgid ""
"If you use `Claude Code <https://claude.com/claude-code>`_, start here: "
"the ``pc`` plugin adds skills that generate parts, assemblies and 2D "
"sketches, describe and search what a package already has, and install the"
" command line tools below for you."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/installation.rst:20
msgid ""
"Then ``/pc:setup`` puts ``pc`` on this machine -- and, when it is run "
"from a Visual Studio Code or VSCodium terminal, :ref:`the extension "
"<vscode-extension>` into that editor -- ``/pc:init`` starts a package, "
"and ``/pc:gen a mounting bracket with four M4 holes`` writes the CAD "
"script, renders four views of what came out and checks them against what "
"was asked. The skills run the same commands documented in :doc:`cli`, so "
"nothing they produce depends on the agent that produced it."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/installation.rst:28
msgid ""
"This repository is the marketplace -- there is no hosted catalog to "
"search for PartCAD in. The ``plugin-dist`` branch is republished by every"
" release and contains no symlinks, which is what makes it install "
"identically on Windows."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/installation.rst:32
msgid "Two other ways to install the same plugin:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/installation.rst:34
msgid ""
"``/plugin marketplace add partcad/partcad`` reads the catalog out of the "
"source tree. That copy shares its skills with the vendor-neutral library "
"through a symlink, so it needs a checkout where git created one -- on "
"Windows, ``git config core.symlinks true`` before cloning."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/installation.rst:37
msgid ""
"Every `release <https://github.com/partcad/partcad/releases>`_ carries a "
"``pc-<version>.zip``, and ``claude --plugin-url <url>`` loads one for a "
"single session. That is how to try a version without installing it."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/installation.rst:41
msgid ""
"The plugin is versioned with everything else in the release that "
"publishes it, so the plugin and the ``pc`` command line tool state the "
"same version when they came from the same release."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/installation.rst:46
msgid ""
"The skills are plain `Agent Skills "
"<https://code.claude.com/docs/en/skills>`_ -- a directory of ``SKILL.md``"
" files -- and the plugin is a thin wrapper that ships them to Claude "
"Code. Any other agent that reads ``SKILL.md`` can use the same library, "
"from ``ai-agents/common/skills`` in the repository. It also ships inside "
"the ``partcad`` wheel, and ``pc init`` installs it into the repository it"
" creates a package in -- so there is nothing to install here if you have "
"PartCAD already."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/installation.rst:54
msgid "Command line tools"
msgstr "命令行工具"

#: ../../source/installation.rst:56
msgid ""
"PartCAD command line tools are implemented in Python and, in theory, "
"available on all platforms where Python is available. However, it is only"
" getting tested on Linux, macOS and Windows."
msgstr ""
"PartCAD 命令行工具使用 Python 实现，理论上可在所有支持 Python 的平台上使用。不过，目前仅在 Linux、macOS 和 "
"Windows 上进行过测试。"

#: ../../source/installation.rst:66
msgid ""
"One package is everything: the ``pc`` command line tool, the Python "
"module, and the ``partcad-json-rpc`` service the editor extensions talk "
"to. ``partcad-cli`` used to be a separate package and is now a thin one "
"that just pulls ``partcad`` in, so ``pip install partcad-cli`` still "
"works if you have it written down somewhere."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/installation.rst:74
#, fuzzy
msgid ""
"No Python on the machine, or no interest in maintaining a Python "
"environment? Install the :ref:`standalone command line tools <standalone-"
"cli>` instead. They are the same tools, shipped with their own "
"interpreter. There is also a :ref:`snap package <snap-package>` for "
"Linux, not published yet."
msgstr ""
"机器上没有 Python，或者不想维护一套 Python 环境？那就改为安装 :ref:`独立命令行工具 <standalone-cli>` "
"。它们是完全相同的工具，只是随附了自带的解释器。"

#: ../../source/installation.rst:81
msgid ""
"PartCAD works best when `conda <https://docs.conda.io/>`_ is installed. "
"If that doesn't help (e.g. macOS+arm64) then try ``mamba``. On Windows, "
"PartCAD must be used inside a ``conda`` environment."
msgstr ""
"在安装了 `conda <https://docs.conda.io/>`_ 的情况下，PartCAD 的效果最好。如果这没有帮助（例如 "
"macOS+arm64），那么可以尝试 ``mamba`` 。在 Windows 上，PartCAD 必须在 ``conda`` 环境中使用。"

#: ../../source/installation.rst:85
msgid ""
"This applies to the wheels. The :ref:`standalone command line tools "
"<standalone-cli>`, the :ref:`snap <snap-package>` and the :ref:`PartCAD "
"IDE <partcad-ide>` carry a conda of their own and need none installed."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/installation.rst:91
msgid ""
"On Ubuntu, try ``apt install libcairo2-dev`` if ``pip install`` fails to "
"install ``cairo``."
msgstr ""
"在 Ubuntu 上，如果 ``pip install`` 无法安装 ``cairo`` ，可以尝试 ``apt install "
"libcairo2-dev`` 。"

#: ../../source/installation.rst:95
msgid ""
"Git does not need to be installed. PartCAD talks to git servers itself, "
"through the ``libgit2`` library that comes with its dependencies, so "
"packages imported from git repositories are cloned and updated without "
"the ``git`` command line tool. Where git is installed, PartCAD still "
"reads its configuration: see :ref:`git-configuration`."
msgstr ""
"无需安装 Git。PartCAD 通过随其依赖一起提供的 ``libgit2`` 库自行与 git 服务器通信，因此从 git 仓库导入的包无需 "
"``git`` 命令行工具即可完成克隆和更新。在已安装 git 的情况下，PartCAD 仍会读取它的配置：请参见 :ref:`git-"
"configuration` 。"

#: ../../source/installation.rst:100
msgid "The commands and options supported by PartCAD CLI:"
msgstr "PartCAD CLI 所支持的命令和选项："

#: ../../source/installation.rst:155
msgid ""
"Common options apply to every command, including ``-v``/``-q`` to raise "
"or lower verbosity, ``--no-ansi`` for plain-text logs, and ``-p PATH`` to"
" select the package (a ``partcad.yaml`` file or a directory that contains"
" one). Run ``pc <command> --help`` to see the options for any command."
msgstr ""
"通用选项适用于每一条命令，包括用于提高或降低详细程度的 ``-v`` / ``-q`` 、用于输出纯文本日志的 ``--no-ansi`` "
"，以及用于选择包（一个 ``partcad.yaml`` 文件或包含该文件的目录）的 ``-p PATH`` 。运行 ``pc <command>"
" --help`` 即可查看任意命令的选项。"

#: ../../source/installation.rst:159
msgid "For a full command reference, see :doc:`cli`."
msgstr "有关完整的命令参考，请参见 :doc:`cli` 。"

#: ../../source/installation.rst:166
msgid "Standalone command line tools (no Python)"
msgstr "独立命令行工具（无需 Python）"

#: ../../source/installation.rst:168
msgid ""
"The standalone build is the same ``pc`` and ``partcad`` commands, "
"packaged with their own Python interpreter and every dependency they "
"need. Nothing is installed into a Python environment, because no Python "
"environment is involved: there is nothing to activate, nothing to keep on"
" the right version, and nothing to break the next time some other tool "
"upgrades Python."
msgstr ""
"独立构建版本就是相同的 ``pc`` 和 ``partcad`` 命令，只是将它们与自带的 Python "
"解释器以及所需的每一项依赖打包在了一起。它不会向任何 Python 环境中安装任何东西，因为整个过程根本不涉及 Python "
"环境：没有需要激活的环境，没有需要保持在正确版本的东西，下次某个其他工具升级 Python 时也不会有任何东西被破坏。"

#: ../../source/installation.rst:173
msgid ""
"Use it if Python is not installed, if the Python that is installed "
"belongs to the operating system and should be left alone, or if PartCAD "
"is simply a tool to run rather than a library to program against. Use the"
" wheels instead if you want to ``import partcad`` from your own scripts."
msgstr ""
"如果没有安装 Python，或者已安装的 Python 属于操作系统、不应去动它，又或者对你来说 PartCAD "
"只是一个要运行的工具而非用于编程的库，那么就使用它。如果你想在自己的脚本中 ``import partcad`` ，则应改用 wheel 包。"

#: ../../source/installation.rst:178 ../../source/installation.rst:515
msgid "Install"
msgstr "安装"

#: ../../source/installation.rst:180 ../../source/installation.rst:517
msgid "On Linux and macOS:"
msgstr "在 Linux 和 macOS 上："

#: ../../source/installation.rst:186
msgid ""
"That downloads the bundle for the current operating system and "
"architecture from the latest `GitHub release "
"<https://github.com/partcad/partcad/releases>`_, verifies its checksum, "
"unpacks it into ``~/.local/share/partcad/<version>``, and links ``pc`` "
"and ``partcad`` into ``~/.local/bin``. Nothing else on the system is "
"touched, and no ``sudo`` is asked for. If ``~/.local/bin`` is not on your"
" ``PATH``, the installer says so and prints the line to add."
msgstr ""
"该命令会从最新的 `GitHub 发布版本 <https://github.com/partcad/partcad/releases>`_ "
"下载适用于当前操作系统和架构的捆绑包，校验其校验和，将其解压到 ``~/.local/share/partcad/<version>`` ，并将 "
"``pc`` 和 ``partcad`` 链接到 ``~/.local/bin`` 。系统上的其他任何内容都不会被改动，也不会要求 "
"``sudo`` 权限。如果 ``~/.local/bin`` 不在你的 ``PATH`` 中，安装程序会告知这一点，并打印出需要添加的那一行。"

#: ../../source/installation.rst:192
msgid ""
"Most of the bundle is the OpenSCAD it carries, so that is what its size "
"follows: the Linux arm64 build, which carries none, is roughly half the "
"size of the others. It carries no CAD kernel: PartCAD builds every shape "
"in a sandbox it provisions itself -- and it carries the conda that "
"provisions it, so nothing has to be installed first, and the ``conda`` "
"sandbox is what you get rather than the ``venv`` fallback the wheels use "
"when there is no conda (see :ref:`python-sandbox`). ``pc healthcheck`` "
"reports what this machine is missing."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/installation.rst:198
#, fuzzy
msgid ""
"Supported platforms are Linux on x86_64 and arm64, and macOS on Apple "
"silicon and on Intel. Windows is covered by the ``.zip`` archives under "
":ref:`manual installation <standalone-manual>`."
msgstr ""
"受支持的平台为 x86_64 架构上的 Linux，以及 Apple 芯片上的 macOS。Windows 则由 :ref:`手动安装 "
"<standalone-manual>` 一节中的 ``.zip`` 归档文件来覆盖。"

#: ../../source/installation.rst:203
msgid ""
"There is one build per supported *operating system version*, not one per "
"operating system. A frozen bundle links against the C library and the "
"system frameworks of the machine that built it, so it runs there and on "
"anything newer, and on nothing older -- a single \"Linux\" build would "
"quietly mean \"whichever Linux the builder happened to be\". Every "
"release publishes a manifest, ``platforms.json``, saying which builds it "
"carries; the installer reads it, works out which of them this machine can"
" run, and downloads that:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/installation.rst:216
msgid ""
"The Ubuntu names are not a requirement to run Ubuntu. Any Linux "
"distribution can run these bundles; what differs between the two is the "
"minimum glibc, and a machine the installer cannot identify as Ubuntu is "
"offered the 22.04 build, which has the lower floor. Pass ``--platform`` "
"to install a specific one."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/installation.rst:220
msgid ""
"macOS has one build per architecture rather than one per macOS version, "
"because a bundle built on macOS 15 runs on macOS 15 and on macOS 26 alike"
" -- both are built and installation-tested on both releases before every "
"publish. On Apple silicon that is the ``arm64`` archive; on an Intel Mac,"
" the ``x86_64`` one."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/installation.rst:224
msgid ""
"Windows is one build rather than one per Windows version, because there "
"is nothing to choose between: the split exists so that a machine can be "
"compared against it, and Windows offers no such comparison -- nor the "
"glibc-style floor that would make one matter. It runs on Windows 10 and "
"later."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/installation.rst:228
msgid ""
"Releases made before ``platforms.json`` existed cannot be resolved this "
"way: there is no way to know from this machine which builds such a "
"release carries. Install the latest release, or name the build with "
"``--platform``."
msgstr ""

